🚀 Q4 — Find Minimum and Maximum Numbers

🎗️ 4.1 Problem Statement

You are given a List<Integer> containing positive and negative integers.

Using Java Streams, find:

The minimum number
The maximum number

Your solution should:

👉 Use the Stream API.
🔴 Correctly handle positive and negative numbers.
🔴 Correctly handle duplicate values.
🔴 Correctly handle an empty list.
🔴 Return an appropriate result when the list is empty.
🔴 Do not modify the original list.

🎗️ 4.2 Input / Output

👉 Input : numbers = [10, 25, -5, 40, 15, 30, 8, 25]
👉 Expected Output : Minimum = -5 Maximum = 40

Because:

Minimum:
-5 is the smallest number.

Maximum:
40 is the largest number.

🎗️ 4.3 Your Task

Write the Java Stream solution.
You can provide:

🔴 Your primary Stream approach.
🔴 Any alternative Stream-based approaches only.
🔴 Empty-list handling.
🔴 Time and space complexity, if you want to attempt them.
